# {{ENTRY_NAME}}

The one skill of {{PLUGIN_NAME}} a person types. Its areas are for agents to
call and stay out of the slash menu, so this is how a person finds the one
they want.

## With a person and no arguments

TODO(author): the questions to ask, at most four, each with two to four
options, so that every area sits behind exactly one option. Then, for the
area chosen: say in a line what it does, ask which of its uses they want, and
hand off once.

## With arguments, or with nobody to ask

Ask nothing. Name the area and the route that fit the task, and hand off.

## The areas

| Area | Use it to | Routes |
| --- | --- | --- |
{{AREA_ROWS}}

## Handing off

Call the area with the Skill tool, the route as the first word of its
arguments: `{{PLUGIN_NAME}}:<area>` with `<route> <the task>`. One hand-off
per run. To explain an area without starting it, read its route table; never
call it for that.
